data floor_skip_control_fixture_exclusion_note: String = "test/fixture/floor_skip/ is excluded from tree-wide discovery at DIR grain (parent ruling 2026-07-11: a fixture that WANTS witness enrollment is mis-homed by definition, and file-grain exclusion invites the next control fixture to repeat the landmine). These fixtures exist to be driven by floor_skip_discovery_witness's explicit rosters, not as corpus witnesses: falsifier_divergence_control_test.dag carries a BY-DESIGN red row (falsifier_red_control_holds returns false to prove the divergence attribution channel), so any completed full-corpus run - the nightly falsifier, or a PR whose diff touches its import closure - would red on a row whose red is the control's specification, and a permanent by-design divergence would also make the falsifier's 8-clean-window retirement criterion unsatisfiable; live_tree_declared_test.dag declares ReadsLiveTree as a control, so as a corpus row it would be a permanent never-skip cost with no enforcement value. Genuine corpus witnesses that were mis-homed here have been re-homed under test/claim/ (provenance_fail_closed_contract_test, live_tree_collision_test). Explicit-roster runs (the floor_skip bin) are unaffected: witness exclusions apply to discovery only."

data enforcement_coverage_exclusion_note: String = "The three enforcement coverage witnesses (enforcement/cost_coverage_witness_test.dag, enforcement/grammar_coverage_witness_test.dag, enforcement_live_witness_test.dag) are operator-ruled OFFLINE (2026-07-11). Receipt: their *_live fns read the corpus as data (live-tree rosters), so the PR-A never-predict-skip rule for live-tree rows made them run on EVERY wide PR regardless of diff; the block cost 22.0 min (main run 29137081535, busy fleet) and 21.0 min (PR run 29142398465, quiet fleet) of the 60-minute floor budget - about 35 percent - and their allocation ramp feeds the ~15GiB slot memory.high throttle that turns the floor tail into swap-speed work. Their input is corpus-denominated (the InputEnvelope axis, not layer span): per-PR admission wants a declared bounded envelope, which these rows cannot declare today. Offlining required TWO edits (cursor review catch, same PR): the discovery exclusion rows here AND removing the explicit CommitCheckEnrollment for enforcement_live_witness_test.dag in gunbc.commit_workflow - explicit roster rows merge after discovery with no exclusion filter (cli_run.rs explicit_entries dedup), and that is correct: an explicitly declared row should run, so offlining one means deleting its declaration, never teaching exclusions to veto the roster (a second authority). Run them via the local recipe: claim_batch --source-root dag --source-root src/v2 --entry <entry> per fn (all pure reads, no --wet needed). Dissolve-on: witness rows declare InputEnvelope/CostEnvelope and the scheduled (nightly) lane admits corpus-input rows under its own budget - then re-enroll consciously through the floor owner's lane; the affected-set-falsifier cadence covers interim drift."

data accumulator_copy_roster_gate_exclusion_note: String = "The three accumulator_copy_roster_gate*_test.dag witnesses are operator-ruled OFFLINE (2026-07-10: the gate is ~15m of serial interpreted resolve; run it via the claim_batch recipe in v2.lens.complexity_accumulator_copy.roster_gate). Excluded from discovery because the flip's selection cannot see them honestly either way: file_gate reads its roster targets via filesystem_read at runtime — a data dependency invisible to resolve-closure attribution — and the live-scan classifier reads only entry-file text, so the rows would be intermittently selected by lens/std-closure PRs (cost, against the ruling) while never firing on roster-target-only PRs (no enforcement). Dissolve-on: resolved-graph memoization receipts land AND the live-read classification walks the import closure; then re-enroll consciously through the floor owner's lane."

data lever_a_local_receipt_witness_exclusion_note: String = "dag/test/claim/lever_a_local_receipt_witness_test.dag is operator-ruled OFFLINE (2026-07-11: witness_touched_path_dispositions_hold cold-scans compile_clean_shard_entry_paths via module_declaration_facts once per scoped disposition row — O(rows) full dag entry-tree walks, 85m+ CI timeout / OOM when selection runs it after lens_verdict on cli_run.dag PRs; run via scripts/lever_a_local_verify.sh). Excluded from discovery for the same structural reason as accumulator_copy_roster_gate: the scoped rows read the shard roster at runtime — invisible to import-closure attribution — so skip-before-resolve cannot honestly bound cost. Dissolve-on: single-roster memo in tools.dag_compile_clean_scope lands AND live-read classification walks import closure for module_declaration_facts consumers; then re-enroll through the floor owner's lane."

data whole_tree_strict_resolve_exclusion_substrings: List<String> = [
  "test/fixture/",
  "/test/",
  "nat_semiring_rung",
  "lens/application/empty_required_lenses_skip_gate.dag",
  "lens/application/rejecting_lens_blocks_before_compile.dag"
]

fn whole_tree_resolve_exclusion_substrings() -> List<String> {
  concat(witness_exclusion_substrings, whole_tree_strict_resolve_exclusion_substrings)
}

fn witness_layer_source_flag_for_root(root: String, shell_path_prefix: String) -> String {
  match shell_path_prefix {
    "" => concat(" --source-root ", root)
    p => concat(" --source-root ", concat(p, concat(root, "\"")))
  }
}

fn witness_layer_source_flags_with_shell_path_prefix(roots: List<String>, shell_path_prefix: String) -> String {
  fold(roots, init: "", f: (acc, r) => concat(acc, witness_layer_source_flag_for_root(root: r, shell_path_prefix: shell_path_prefix)))
}

fn witness_layer_source_flags(roots: List<String>) -> String {
  witness_layer_source_flags_with_shell_path_prefix(roots, shell_path_prefix: "")
}

fn witness_layer_source_flags_rooted(roots: List<String>) -> String {
  witness_layer_source_flags_with_shell_path_prefix(roots, shell_path_prefix: "\"$ROOT/")
}

fn witness_layer_scan_flags() -> String {
  fold(witness_discovery_scan_dirs, init: "", f: (acc, d) => concat(acc, concat(" --scan-dir ", d)))
}
